{
  "id": "reading-retired-offline-review",
  "title": "Reading cards retired by a setting while a device reviews one offline (ADR-035)",
  "covers": [
    "ADR-035: cards.reading_enabled is an ordinary settings.set register; retiring emits no card op",
    "ADR-035: an offline review of a retired reading card is kept and replays on its own card",
    "ADR-035: the reading review never feeds the meaning card"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "A creates vocab note N with meaning card M and reading card R (reading cards were still on: A set cards.reading_enabled = true at T+5).",
    "B pulls everything up to seq 4 and goes offline. At T+30 B answers R (Again).",
    "At T+40 A turns reading cards off (settings.set false, the UI toggle) and syncs; at T+50 A answers M. No card op is minted: R is not suspended, deleted or merged.",
    "B comes back and pushes its T+30 review of R. The server accepts it as usual (seq 7); every replica appends it and replays R, whose cache moves to learning. M's replay set holds only A's review.",
    "Whatever the arrival order, the setting ends false (T+40 beats T+5) and R stays live with its review. Derived state (not modelled by tools/model.py): every QueueBuilder ignores R (QueueBuilder rule 0) and word_status.auto_status of entry 1358280 is derived from M alone (learning), not from R; turning the setting back on would show R again with this history."
  ],
